 n= 4096: A1 smaller than BEHW for T < None  (note: 'whenever T <~ log2(2n)' = 13); at T=10: A1=0.036, BEHW=0.122
 n=16384: A1 smaller than BEHW for T < None  (note: 'whenever T <~ log2(2n)' = 15); at T=10: A1=0.009, BEHW=0.033

## 7. Random correlated dictionaries: (SC) race with exits, (LS) depth-one race
 SC (40 trials): total exits from the saturated set = 130;
   max | ||c||_1 - <R,f>_n | = 2.66e-14 (Theorem A2.4, Theta=1); max |S_m - <R,g_m>_n| = 2.46e-14;
   max (|S|-Theta) = 0.00e+00 (Lemma 2.2(3)); max |U_m| on support = 5.44e-16; chain <= ||R|| <= tau asserted
 LS (40 trials): max over events of T / (kappa tau^2) = 0.715 (Theorem A2.3 needs <= 1)

## 8. race_bounds.py: S[~dormant] = [sign[m] for m in active] assigns in index order, not in 'active' order
 active=[4, 1], sign={4: 1.0, 1: -1.0} -> S[1]=1.0, S[4]=-1.0 (should be -1, +1). Harmless in LS (fired clocks unused); in SC it would corrupt the clock of a gate that later exits.

## 9. Proposition A3.4(3): first-occurrence validation, adaptive memorizer, Monte Carlo
 mean of (1/K) sum [L(h_s_k) - loss on first occurrence] = 0.0007 +- 0.0007 (should be ~0); P(gap > sqrt(log(1/0.05)/(2K))) = 0.0015 (should be <= 0.05)
